    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class \u2014 the only test in the project) passes, and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `registrationDate` behavior for owners: when no registration date is supplied on `POST /api/owners`, it defaults to the server's current date, and it's always returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this puts the field on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) so a supplied date is captured, and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`) so it's read back. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the mapped owner has none, preserving a supplied value otherwise.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to `owners` in the hsqldb (used by the test profile), h2, mysql, and postgres schema files. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column was required there; the others were updated for consistency.\n\nBoth scenarios are green: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (keeps `2020-06-15`).",
